 "prompt": "Use only the kibana tools.\n\nWork on Kibana's web-logs sample data (data view 'Kibana Sample Data Logs', index kibana_sample_data_logs). Do these steps in order:\n1. Describe the data view 'Kibana Sample Data Logs': look up its fields and name its time field.\n2. Build a dashboard titled 'LOC-4435972e Web logs' on that data view with exactly two panels: the number of requests over time, and the number of requests by HTTP response code.\n3. Create an alert rule named 'LOC-4435972e 5xx errors' on the web-logs data for the signal of the response-code panel: it checks every minute and fires when more than 10 server errors arrive within 5 minutes. Count all server errors: every request whose response code is anywhere from 500 to 599. The rule must be enabled when you finish: if it is created disabled, enable it.\n4. Edit the response-code panel of that dashboard: change its title to 'Responses by code'. Then read the alert rule back and check whether it is enabled.\n\nWhen every step is done, end your reply with these two lines:\nTIME_FIELD: <the data view's time field>\nRULE_ENABLED: <yes or no, as you read it back>",
